# Gott, wie gross ist deine Guete, BWV 462 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Sacred song No. 26 in the Mutopia edition (Franz Wullner's 1893
# edition of Schemelli's Musicalisches Gesang-Buch, Leipzig 1736); text
# by Schemelli himself ("God, how great is your goodness"). Melody and
# figured bass; the bass here is the printed one, the figures not played.
#
# Character: a song of thanks in 4/4, B-flat major, the melody in
# quarters with two-note eighth slurs, the bass in walking eighths. Warm
# and steady, like a chorale with more movement.
#
# Time signature: 4/4, 16 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI; the
# first note is on the downbeat. The first four bars are repeated
# (Mutopia notes the form "AABA"; the second couplet of text goes on the
# repeat); the other twelve are not. The MIDI does not play the repeat;
# it is written out with `play`.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 72. One stanza as performed is 20 bars, 80 quarters.
# MusicBrainz track times: Aki Matsui and Masaaki Suzuki 1:43; Alice
# Babs 1:57; Elisabeth Speiser 2:01; Klaus Mertens and Ton Koopman 2:07;
# Sibylla Rubens 1:40. The song has four stanzas and I could not find how
# many each recording sings, so these do not convert reliably (one stanza
# would give about 45, two about 90). 72 is my judgment, near the Mutopia
# MIDI's 70: the walking bass eighths move at 144 a minute, steady but
# not hurried, and each line can breathe at its cadence.
#
# Structure (Mutopia score and figures; one line of text per four bars):
#   1-4    line 1, B-flat major, cadence in B-flat (bar 4); repeated for
#          line 2 ("Ach, wie labt sich mein Gemuete")
#   5-8    line 3, troubled ("Wenn mich etwas will betrueben"): to G
#          minor, half close on D (bar 8)
#   9-12   line 4 ("zeiget sie von deinem Lieben"): through C minor to a
#          cadence on C (bar 12)
#   13-16  line 5 ("und Trotz bieten kann der Hoelle"): home to B-flat,
#          the close of the opening lines returning
#
# Bars as performed (after `play`):
#   A 1-4, A repeat 5-8, then score bars 5-16 as 9-20 (score x is x+4).
#
# Plan: shaped by the text, terraced by line: mf, the repeat mp, the
# troubled line mp, the line of comfort mf, the defiant last line f.
# Each line's cadence bar gets a short breath, as a congregation does.

tempo 72
play 1-4 1-16

voice mid 0        # two voices only: no middle voice to set back

dyn 1 mf           # bars 1-4: line 1
dyn 5 mp           # bars 5-8: the repeat, line 2
dyn 9 mp           # bars 9-12 (score 5-8): the troubled line
dyn 13 mf          # bars 13-16 (score 9-12): the line of comfort
dyn 17 f           # bars 17-20 (score 13-16): defiance, and home

broaden 4 0.9      # line ends: cadence in B-flat
broaden 8 0.9      # the same after the repeat
broaden 12 0.88    # score bar 8: half close on D
broaden 16 0.9     # score bar 12: cadence on C

rit 1.5 0.7        # the final cadence in B-flat
